  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThursday-Friday:\nCooler and lower humidity persist through Thursday, with 10-20%\nchances for light rain/sprinkles on Thursday morning/afternoon.\nAs this weak wave passes through the area, another wave is on\nthe horizon. This next system takes shape Thursday night into\nFriday morning, and will feature stronger forcing and better\nmoisture return. The highest rain chances (40-70%) are currently\ndepicted across portions of west central into central MO through\nFriday morning. An initial analysis suggests that scattered\nshowers and thunderstorms overspread the area, with the primary\nhazards being lightning and localized heavy rainfall. PWATs\nupwards of 2+ inches will support efficient rainfall rates, and\nany locations that see repeated rounds of thunderstorms may be\nsubject to localized heavy rainfall and flash flooding. However,\nit will be tough to pin down these exact corridors of heavier\namounts until mesoscale features become more apparent. Rain\nchances (30-60%) linger through Friday and slowly sink south\ninto the rest of southern MO. Rain chances gradually diminish\ninto Saturday morning, though it is worth noting there is still\nsome uncertainty on the exact timing of the passing shortwaves.\n\nSaturday-Tuesday:\nAs we progress into the weekend, a strong ridge begins to build\nout of the western CONUS. This will support increasing mid-\nlevel heights, and a return of hot and humid conditions. There\nwill be a bit of gradient from west to east this weekend as a\nresult of being on the eastern periphery of the ridge. Highs\nSaturday are progged to vary from upper 80s/lower 90s (east) to\nmiddle/upper 90s (west). The return of this heat will be\naccompanied by minimal rain chances, unless we get into the\neastern edge of ridge runners. For now, rain chances remain less\nthan 10% late this weekend into early next week. Additionally,\nconfidence is increasing that the hot temperatures and humidity\nbuild further into early next week. By Sunday into Monday,\nportions of southeast KS into southwest MO are progged to see\nhighs reach upper 90s to around 100+. Meanwhile, heat index\nvalues climb into the 100 to 110 degree range. This may support\nthe need for heat headlines in subsequent forecast updates this\nweekend.",
